Provenance
==========

Everything in this repository is under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

24 of the 27 role files began as the "Locus Agent Template Pack v1.0.0" (2026-09-18), a
content pack generated for this repository's author from their own screenshots of the Locus
application. That pack carries no copyright line, no author attribution, and no license,
and its own metadata describes its contents as "original suggested content" and "not
official built-in behavior" of Locus. It is not Locus's product documentation and not a
third party's work product — so there is no separate rights holder to license from, and the
MIT grant above covers it.

The adaptation here replaced that pack's runtime, mode, memory-scope, and access-level
vocabulary with Claude Code's equivalents and dropped its grading metadata. The working
methods, deliverables, boundaries, and mode guidance remain substantially the pack's text.

Three roles are original to this repository: version-control, data-engineer, and
incident-responder.

"Locus" is the name of the application those templates were originally written for
(locushost.co). It is used here only to say where the text came from; this project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Locus.

If that pack in fact came from someone else who claims rights in it, this notice is wrong
and the 24 derived roles need their permission or a rewrite.
